# *registry not found*. Two toolsets ship under one installer now, so one
# number means two things across that seam: no caller may read a number without
# knowing which command produced it.
#
# A REFUSAL FROM HERE IS NOT A CAPABILITY SIGNAL. `die`'s default exit is also
# 2, so an unknown argument and a genuine refusal are the same number. A caller
# that wants to know whether `wip` exists PROBES `openRepoTools --help` for the
# verb pair, never an exit code — read the other way round, a genuine refusal
# with the administrator's `gh repo create` block already on the terminal would
# be reported as "no such subcommand", and a degradation recipe printed over
# the top of the one thing the person needed. opensoft/workBenches#68 probes
# `--help` for exactly this reason.

