    cannot READ is not one it may stage over — step 8's \`git add\` would replace it with this
    run's copy, silently, and commit that. Nothing beyond this run's own template bytes was
    written into that checkout, and nothing already staged was changed.
    Repair that object (\`git fsck\`), or commit, stash or unstage that path, then re-run:
        openRepoTools wip init"
					[ "$staged_mode" = "100644" ] ||
						die "$checkout has $rel staged with mode $staged_mode, and every file in
    $SHAPE_REPOSITORY's $WIP_TEMPLATE_DIR is a plain 100644 — this command has never chmod'ed
    anything it wrote, so a mode of its own at that path is somebody's own \`git add\`, not an
    earlier run's leftover, whatever the staged bytes say. Staging this run's copy over it would
